# KernelSU-Legacy Integration Guide (v1.1.1)

This guide provides step-by-step instructions to manually integrate **KernelSU-Legacy v1.1.1** into the `redbull` kernel source (`kernel/google/redbull`).

---

## 1. Navigate to Source Root

Ensure you are in the root directory of your kernel source before proceeding:

```bash
cd kernel/google/redbull


---

2. Automatic Patching

Run the following command to download and execute the official setup script.
This will pull the KernelSU source into your driver tree and apply the necessary hooks:

curl -LSs "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KernelSU-Legacy/KernelSU-Legacy/v1.1.1/kernel/setup.sh" | bash -


---

3. Enable Kernel Configuration (Defconfig)

To enable KernelSU in your build, you must add the specific configs to your target defconfig file.
For the redbull device, the target is usually:

arch/arm64/configs/vendor/redbull_defconfig

Run these commands to append the required flags:

echo "CONFIG_KSU=y" >> arch/arm64/configs/vendor/redbull_defconfig
echo "CONFIG_KSU_LEGACY=y" >> arch/arm64/configs/vendor/redbull_defconfig

> Note Ensure that CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y is also present in your defconfig, as it is required for KernelSU to function properly.




---

4. Manual Verification (Optional)

If the automated script fails to modify the build system, ensure the following lines exist in your driver files:

drivers/Kconfig

Add this at the end of the file:

source "drivers/kernelsu/Kconfig"

drivers/Makefile

Add this at the end of the file:

obj-y += kernelsu/


---

5. Build Instructions

Once integrated, proceed with your standard compilation process:

# Clean previous builds
make clean
make mrproper

# Start the build (example)
# make vendor/redbull_defconfig
# make -j$(nproc)


---

Version Metadata

KernelSU-Legacy Version: 1.1.1

Target Kernel Tree: kernel/google/redbull

Architecture: ARM64
